\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\title{Alternating forms and a determinant square}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{The signed matching formula for the
[Pfaffian](fdip-008I) has integer coefficients. It can therefore
be compared with the [ring divided coefficients](fdip-00TF)
before any factorial is inverted. Applying that comparison to
a perfect alternating form and a compatible kernel gives a
basis-independent square root of the determinant.}

